 9, and 10)': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ["The specific mathematical formulations used to quantify the difference between the student and teacher models' outputs during the Transformer distillation process. These equations define the objectives for knowledge transfer from BERT to TinyBERT, encompassing various distillation targets like hidden states, attention matrices, and prediction layers."], 'source_chunk_index': [1]}, 'Layer Mapping Function (g(m) = 3 × m)': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A function that determines the correspondence between layers in the teacher BERT model and the student TinyBERT model. In this case, it specifies that TinyBERT learns from every 3 layers of the BERT BASE model, enabling knowledge transfer across different architectural depths.'], 'source_chunk_index': [1]}, 'English Wikipedia': {'type': ['DATASET'], 'description': ['The text corpus used for general distillation in the TinyBERT learning framework.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'CoLA': {'type': ['task', 'dataset'], 'description': ["The Corpus of Linguistic Acceptability, a task within the GLUE benchmark that assesses a model's ability to predict linguistic acceptability judgments.", "A task within the GLUE benchmark used to evaluate TinyBERT's performance."], 'source_chunk_index': [2, 3]}, 'MNLI': {'type': ['task', 'dataset', 'dataset', 'task'], 'description': ['The Multi-Genre Natural Language Inference task, part of the GLUE benchmark, used in ablation studies to evaluate TinyBERT.', 'A dataset used in the ablation studies, part of the GLUE benchmark.', "A task within the GLUE benchmark used to evaluate TinyBERT's performance.", 'A task within the GLUE benchmark, used to evaluate natural language understanding models.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2, 2, 3, 3]}, 'MRPC': {'type': ['task', 'dataset', 'dataset'], 'description': ['The Microsoft Research Paraphrase Corpus, a GLUE benchmark task used in ablation studies.', 'A dataset used in the ablation studies, part of